<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of the Indies</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1524">1524</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of the Indies was the supreme administrative and judicial body for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s American and Asian colonies, established in 1524. It drafted laws, advised the king on appointments and heard appeals. It was the central institution of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>'s colonial government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-the-indies.jpg" alt="Council of the Indies" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown Author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Emblem_of_the_Council_of_the_Indies.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Santa Fe in 1492, divided the non-European world with Portugal by the Treaty of Tordesillas in 1494, and treated the Americas as Castilian possessions: the <b>Council of the Indies</b>, founded in 1524, governed them under Castilian law, and Castilian Spanish became the language of most of the Americas.</blockquote><a href="/empire/crown-of-castile">Crown of Castile · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The VOC's headquarters at Batavia, founded by Coen in 1619 on the north-western coast of Java, served as the capital of an Asian network administered by a Governor-General and <b>Council of the Indies</b> answerable to the Heeren XVII, the company's board of directors in the Netherlands.</blockquote><a href="/empire/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>…the polysynodal regime: the Councils of State and War for foreign policy, the Council of Castile for justice and internal government, the Councils of Aragon, Italy, Portugal and Flanders for those territories, the <b>Council of the Indies</b>, founded in 1524, for the Americas, and the Council of Finance.</blockquote><a href="/empire/habsburg-spain">Habsburg Spain · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>He answered to the <b>Council of the Indies</b> in Spain, and at the end of his term his conduct was examined in a judicial review, the residencia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/new-spain">New Spain · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Council of the Indies</b>, established in 1524, governed the American colonies from Castile, and the colonial legislation it oversaw was later gathered in the Recopilación de Leyes de los Reinos de las Indias (1680), a comprehensive code covering every aspect of colonial administration.</blockquote><a href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The viceroy, appointed by the king on the advice of the <b>Council of the Indies</b>, was the Crown's personal representative: he presided over the Audiencia of Lima, commanded the armed forces, supervised the treasury and exercised royal patronage over the Church.</blockquote><a href="/empire/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
